                        "review": "Lets preface. I dont expect this review to stay up. I see how the devs have handled criticism. I am going to be fair in this review. I doubt it will matter. \n\nIts built on the Unity engine. There have been some really nice games built in Unity. Right now, this isnt one of them. Let's discuss why. \n\nGraphics: Offers multiple options to alter your graphics settings. There is a slight visual difference from the lowest to highest setting. HOwever, it doesnt really matter. The graphics are pretty bad. Stills from this game are its best case scenario. The minute you move, you have flickering textures, massive pop-in, muddy colors, and the whole thing just looks outdated. There is mention of a day night cycle, which yes, is functional and included. Multiple problems here though. Its very short. At night, the game basically becomes unplayable, as its TOO dark. Flashlight mind as well be a candle. Cant see a thing. And yet you still get massive sun flare, as the devs hide the sun, flare included, behind the mountains at night. Awesome. \n\nGameplay: No. You have soldiers shooting you with pinpoint accuracy the minute you turn the corner. Thats fine, I like a challenge. However, heres where the gfx screw you over. You cant find them. Occasionally you will see a muzzle flash, but it doesnt matter. Since everything is muddy and streaky, you cant find anyone. Funny thing is, as the soldiers close in on you, they seem to get less accurate. I spawned once with a soldier right on top of me. Kept shooting me, and I barely got hit. Took out the sniper rifle, scoped his head, and fired. 4 shots to the head later, he died. Realism kids. Realism. \n\nSound: Some of the guns do sound pretty good. Grenandes need help, as the explosions are pretty bad. The rain sound cuts out at least 30 seconds before the rain stops. Other than that, its.. fine? I mean you will be noticing alot more before you worry about the sound. \n\nPerformance: This is where it gets ugly. I get it. Its early access. But guys. Come on. I have 2 GTX 980s, an i7, and 32gb of DDR4 ram. I averaged 15 fps. some spots gave me 20-25, other it became a slide show. I tried the graphics on max, then on min. Nothing. No change. Unity games I have played in the past have had zero issues on my system. I am not expecting things to work from day one flawlessly. But to release a game in this condition is a travesty. \n\nIve tried not to blast this game. I dont want to be \"that guy\" going on and on about an early access game. But this is where early access gets its bad name from. For every ARC and Prison Architect, theres a Second Warfare. Games like this should NOT be greenlit. \n\nFor however long you can see my review, please take my advice.",
